{"Success":true,"Data":{"State":"open","OpenTime":0,"CloseTime":0,"IsApproved":true,"IsPinned":false,"IsDeleted":false,"IsHidden":false,"IsArchived":false,"IsFollowing":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanReply":true,"CanFollow":true,"TotalPosts":15,"QueuedPosts":0,"DeletedPosts":0,"HasUnreadPosts":false,"HasAttachments":false,"Views":2237,"MovedTo":null,"MovedOn":0,"FirstPostId":1900645,"Rating":0,"RatingHits":0,"Starter":{"Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1443808962","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"StartDate":1437129160,"LastPoster":{"Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1443808962","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"PollState":"0","LastVote":0,"ForumId":13,"Preview":{"Id":1900645,"PostDate":1437129160,"PostContent":"Hi Ladies! \u00a0 I really need to vent, and if anyone will understand it will be you. \u00a0 I don't even...","Author":{"Signature":"<div><img src=\"http:\/\/\" alt=\"\"><\/div>\n<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;0\/st\/20160423\/e\/we+leave+for+Mexico%21\/k\/c059\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;32;116\/st\/20160430\/e\/we+say+I+do%21\/k\/8afc\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529<\/a>","Email":"deannaproteau@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1421424569,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1443808962","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"deecol","Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","IsOnline":false}},"Posts":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79405,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5e382e7742d985a39de4418bcf86710a","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hi Ladies!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I really need to vent, and if anyone will understand it will be you.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I don&#039;t even have to say this, we all know that when it comes to destination weddings, some people will be there and book without hesitation, some will say yes and not book, and some will not be able to attend. &amp;nbsp;What I&#039;m finding extremely difficult to process and understand is the complete lack of communication and respect my own family and \"close\" friends have for me and my fianc\u00e9.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We get a group rate and reserve seats, give months of advance warning and in every reminder email I have sent I have expressed that they are more than welcome to make their own accommodations, however they may not get the same price or the hotel may not have room for them when they do decide to book.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;My booking deadline is next week. &amp;nbsp;I have 6 people who have guaranteed me they will book by this date. &amp;nbsp;One of my friends texted me to let me know she&#039;s booking on Saturday, she obviously didn&#039;t read the last email I sent where I let everyone know the agency is closed on weekends, it&#039;s no problem, she can call Monday, but then I thought, shoot - maybe I should let the others know. &amp;nbsp;So I text one of my \"close\" girlfriends, she then asks me \"do we have to pay by October? because I can&#039;t\". &amp;nbsp;No problem, you don&#039;t have to but there is a early booking bonus included in my rate and you will have to pay that if you miss the deadline and told her to feel free to look into other options. &amp;nbsp;She then says \"Your wedding is in April LOL, I don&#039;t get why we have to pay so early, I travel to resorts quite a bit and they&#039;re never sold out in April\". &amp;nbsp;Trying not to be rude I let her know that I am not psychic and have no way of knowing if the price will go up or down, and if the resort will sell out or not, all I did was negotiate a group rate and reserved some seats so my closest family and friends can hold their spot. &amp;nbsp;My fianc\u00e9 has worked in travel all his life, we did a lot of research before choosing this resort and date. &amp;nbsp;The final straw of this conversation: &amp;nbsp;I tell her, I get it, it is an expense and Colin and I need to have our payment in by October too. &amp;nbsp;She says: Oh, you guys have to pay? &amp;nbsp;I just thought you were trying to get a certain amount of people to book so you could get a free trip. &amp;nbsp;It made me feel like I&#039;m being perceived as a scammer and I should not feel like this when I&#039;m trying to plan my wedding. &amp;nbsp;Yes, sometimes we get incentives on trips if a certain number of people book, but if she was such a close friend she would have talked to me about how my wedding plans are going so far and realized I am no where near even getting one comp ticket. &amp;nbsp;It doesn&#039;t matter to me, we are getting married, it&#039;s an expense, a comp would be a bonus but that&#039;s not the reason I arranged a group rate. &amp;nbsp;I let her know that when we looked at this resort for 2015 a couple weeks before our dates it was sold out so she can take her chances, we ended the conversation by her patronizing me \"Oh really? &amp;nbsp;I&#039;ve never seen that, must have been spring breakers. Woooo\" &amp;nbsp;And we agreed for her to look into other options. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m at the point right now where I don&#039;t care. &amp;nbsp;Do what you want.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The other shocker in my current situation is my Dad&#039;s side of the family. &amp;nbsp;He has 5 siblings, they all have kids and some of them have kids. &amp;nbsp;I have always been close with them, they know my dad and I have always had a great relationship especially through my parents divorce and we have always stayed in contact. &amp;nbsp;My Dad will be the only one from his side at my wedding. &amp;nbsp;I understand not being able to afford it, and that is completely okay, but when my cousin got married in Nova Scotia, they all went. &amp;nbsp;Another just got engaged that lives there and I&#039;m sure they will all go. &amp;nbsp;Some are even going down this summer. &amp;nbsp;When I was trying to collect their addresses for my invites it was so difficult, then I send the invitations and I don&#039;t even get a reply, nothing to even say they can&#039;t make it. &amp;nbsp;This really upsets my Dad, so he who is scared to even use a computer posted a FACEBOOK message to his family. &amp;nbsp;No one responded. &amp;nbsp;So now he&#039;s calling everyone individually, and as the declines roll in, I&#039;m not upset, I&#039;m upset with those family members who my dad has spoken to and they still haven&#039;t contacted me, and those family members who he is chasing down, he shouldn&#039;t have to chase them down. &amp;nbsp;He had planned to share a room with one of my cousins, my cousin has ignored every phone call from him, every message from me, but told other family members that he can&#039;t commit right now and will probably book later. &amp;nbsp;Why couldn&#039;t he tell one of us that? &amp;nbsp;My dad was left to find someone to share a room with and luckily a friend of mine from elementary school needed a room-mate. &amp;nbsp;It makes my Dad really upset, which is not fair to him.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Trying not to let it bother me and focus on the fact that we have 32 of our closest family and friends from Canada and the UK with their deposits down. &amp;nbsp;That is more than I could ever ask for.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Thanks for letting me rant :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1900645,"PostDate":1437129160,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hi Ladies!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I really need to vent, and if anyone will understand it will be you.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I don't even have to say this, we all know that when it comes to destination weddings, some people will be there and book without hesitation, some will say yes and not book, and some will not be able to attend. \u00a0What I'm finding extremely difficult to process and understand is the complete lack of communication and respect my own family and \"close\" friends have for me and my fianc\u00e9.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We get a group rate and reserve seats, give months of advance warning and in every reminder email I have sent I have expressed that they are more than welcome to make their own accommodations, however they may not get the same price or the hotel may not have room for them when they do decide to book.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My booking deadline is next week. \u00a0I have 6 people who have guaranteed me they will book by this date. \u00a0One of my friends texted me to let me know she's booking on Saturday, she obviously didn't read the last email I sent where I let everyone know the agency is closed on weekends, it's no problem, she can call Monday, but then I thought, shoot - maybe I should let the others know. \u00a0So I text one of my \"close\" girlfriends, she then asks me \"do we have to pay by October? because I can't\". \u00a0No problem, you don't have to but there is a early booking bonus included in my rate and you will have to pay that if you miss the deadline and told her to feel free to look into other options. \u00a0She then says \"Your wedding is in April LOL, I don't get why we have to pay so early, I travel to resorts quite a bit and they're never sold out in April\". \u00a0Trying not to be rude I let her know that I am not psychic and have no way of knowing if the price will go up or down, and if the resort will sell out or not, all I did was negotiate a group rate and reserved some seats so my closest family and friends can hold their spot. \u00a0My fianc\u00e9 has worked in travel all his life, we did a lot of research before choosing this resort and date. \u00a0The final straw of this conversation: \u00a0I tell her, I get it, it is an expense and Colin and I need to have our payment in by October too. \u00a0She says: Oh, you guys have to pay? \u00a0I just thought you were trying to get a certain amount of people to book so you could get a free trip. \u00a0It made me feel like I'm being perceived as a scammer and I should not feel like this when I'm trying to plan my wedding. \u00a0Yes, sometimes we get incentives on trips if a certain number of people book, but if she was such a close friend she would have talked to me about how my wedding plans are going so far and realized I am no where near even getting one comp ticket. \u00a0It doesn't matter to me, we are getting married, it's an expense, a comp would be a bonus but that's not the reason I arranged a group rate. \u00a0I let her know that when we looked at this resort for 2015 a couple weeks before our dates it was sold out so she can take her chances, we ended the conversation by her patronizing me \"Oh really? \u00a0I've never seen that, must have been spring breakers. Woooo\" \u00a0And we agreed for her to look into other options. \u00a0I'm at the point right now where I don't care. \u00a0Do what you want.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The other shocker in my current situation is my Dad's side of the family. \u00a0He has 5 siblings, they all have kids and some of them have kids. \u00a0I have always been close with them, they know my dad and I have always had a great relationship especially through my parents divorce and we have always stayed in contact. \u00a0My Dad will be the only one from his side at my wedding. \u00a0I understand not being able to afford it, and that is completely okay, but when my cousin got married in Nova Scotia, they all went. \u00a0Another just got engaged that lives there and I'm sure they will all go. \u00a0Some are even going down this summer. \u00a0When I was trying to collect their addresses for my invites it was so difficult, then I send the invitations and I don't even get a reply, nothing to even say they can't make it. \u00a0This really upsets my Dad, so he who is scared to even use a computer posted a FACEBOOK message to his family. \u00a0No one responded. \u00a0So now he's calling everyone individually, and as the declines roll in, I'm not upset, I'm upset with those family members who my dad has spoken to and they still haven't contacted me, and those family members who he is chasing down, he shouldn't have to chase them down. \u00a0He had planned to share a room with one of my cousins, my cousin has ignored every phone call from him, every message from me, but told other family members that he can't commit right now and will probably book later. \u00a0Why couldn't he tell one of us that? \u00a0My dad was left to find someone to share a room with and luckily a friend of mine from elementary school needed a room-mate. \u00a0It makes my Dad really upset, which is not fair to him.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Trying not to let it bother me and focus on the fact that we have 32 of our closest family and friends from Canada and the UK with their deposits down. \u00a0That is more than I could ever ask for.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Thanks for letting me rant <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><img src=\"http:\/\/\" alt=\"\"><\/div>\n<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;0\/st\/20160423\/e\/we+leave+for+Mexico%21\/k\/c059\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;32;116\/st\/20160430\/e\/we+say+I+do%21\/k\/8afc\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529<\/a>","Email":"deannaproteau@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1421424569,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1443808962","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"deecol","Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"68.146.146.173","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79405,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"2f3cba267014c76739ef935d1d4c1392","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hugs!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You are always welcome to vent here, I think amongst all of us we have seen it all.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I know this doesn&#039;t make your situation any easier - or help with your frustration - but this seems to be par for the course with weddings, especially destination weddings.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;All you can do is send friendly reminders and leave it at that. It&#039;s frustrating, maddening, upsetting, etc. but there is nothing you can do :( &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Take comfort in the fact that 32 of your friends and family have made the commitment to go and focus on those relationships right now.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We had issues with some friends and some family - even Shawn&#039;s dad dug his heals in HARD....&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Good luck!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;ps - I did shake my head when your friend assumed you wouldn&#039;t have to pay. That is NOT why people do group bookings!!! OMG!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1900662,"PostDate":1437145809,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hugs!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>You are always welcome to vent here, I think amongst all of us we have seen it all.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I know this doesn't make your situation any easier - or help with your frustration - but this seems to be par for the course with weddings, especially destination weddings.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>All you can do is send friendly reminders and leave it at that. It's frustrating, maddening, upsetting, etc. but there is nothing you can do <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/> \u00a0 \u00a0Take comfort in the fact that 32 of your friends and family have made the commitment to go and focus on those relationships right now.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We had issues with some friends and some family - even Shawn's dad dug his heals in HARD....\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Good luck!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>ps - I did shake my head when your friend assumed you wouldn't have to pay. That is NOT why people do group bookings!!! OMG!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399410602,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"50.76.78.161","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79405,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":7,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"02fbc478393e492fbb1b40d43248fa0b","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Your family sounds just like mine! &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m getting married in Playa del Carmen in 4 months and I just found out this week my sisters are going. &amp;nbsp;But they still have NOT booked! &amp;nbsp;Not one person in my family has. &amp;nbsp;I also had a handful of friends that promised 100% they would go and now backed out because they decided to travel elsewhere this year. &amp;nbsp;At least make up a good excuse! &amp;nbsp;Before we booked, we asked my sisters, my cousin and dad if they would go. &amp;nbsp;They all said yes, sure. &amp;nbsp;Then after we book, it&#039;s &#039;I&#039;m not sure I can afford it.&#039; &amp;nbsp;They had 2 years to save! &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;My mom passed away a few years ago and I&#039;m really close with her sisters and my cousins. &amp;nbsp; I see my aunts almost once a week. &amp;nbsp;I have two cousins, those two aunts and an uncle that are not going. &amp;nbsp;And it&#039;s not because of money. &amp;nbsp;It&#039;s because they &#039;poo poo&#039; Mexico. &amp;nbsp;It&#039;s not where they want to go on vacation. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;It really does hurt and it makes you sad. &amp;nbsp;But I am at the point now where I am just focusing on me and my man. &amp;nbsp;And I only talk to the people that are excited for us. &amp;nbsp;As I get older and people get busy and have their own lives, I&#039;ve noticed more and more that people can be bad at communicating and rsvp&#039;ing. &amp;nbsp;Just try to focus on things that you can control. &amp;nbsp;It&#039;s your big day and if those people do not want to be there with you to celebrate, then they wouldn&#039;t be any fun anyways. &amp;nbsp;And if the hotel or flights get sold out, then it&#039;s up to them to figure it out on their own. &amp;nbsp;I know it&#039;s easier said than done, but you will exhaust yourself if you spend all this time hunting people down. &amp;nbsp;I wish you luck and hope some of them start shaping up!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1900664,"PostDate":1437146308,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Your family sounds just like mine! \u00a0I'm getting married in Playa del Carmen in 4 months and I just found out this week my sisters are going. \u00a0But they still have NOT booked! \u00a0Not one person in my family has. \u00a0I also had a handful of friends that promised 100% they would go and now backed out because they decided to travel elsewhere this year. \u00a0At least make up a good excuse! \u00a0Before we booked, we asked my sisters, my cousin and dad if they would go. \u00a0They all said yes, sure. \u00a0Then after we book, it's 'I'm not sure I can afford it.' \u00a0They had 2 years to save! \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My mom passed away a few years ago and I'm really close with her sisters and my cousins. \u00a0 I see my aunts almost once a week. \u00a0I have two cousins, those two aunts and an uncle that are not going. \u00a0And it's not because of money. \u00a0It's because they 'poo poo' Mexico. \u00a0It's not where they want to go on vacation. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It really does hurt and it makes you sad. \u00a0But I am at the point now where I am just focusing on me and my man. \u00a0And I only talk to the people that are excited for us. \u00a0As I get older and people get busy and have their own lives, I've noticed more and more that people can be bad at communicating and rsvp'ing. \u00a0Just try to focus on things that you can control. \u00a0It's your big day and if those people do not want to be there with you to celebrate, then they wouldn't be any fun anyways. \u00a0And if the hotel or flights get sold out, then it's up to them to figure it out on their own. \u00a0I know it's easier said than done, but you will exhaust yourself if you spend all this time hunting people down. \u00a0I wish you luck and hope some of them start shaping up!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"yukka33@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"67.173.124.145","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1392462075,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"Sarahop81","Id":276722,"Name":"Sarahop81","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79405,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":3,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e09631fbda054ddc5a4326979d90f863","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"calgarybride2015\"] Thank you :) &amp;nbsp;That killed me too when she said she thought I would get a free trip. &amp;nbsp;The nerve! &amp;nbsp;I actually read back our conversation because I&#039;m so rattled and realized when she said about having to pay by october she actually said \"why do we have to pay by October, the TRIP isn&#039;t until April\" &amp;nbsp;TRIP! &amp;nbsp;She called it a trip and not my wedding. &amp;nbsp;Maybe I&#039;m reading too much into it and she didn&#039;t mean it that way, but after the convo we had I really think she did. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m 100% going to focus on our 32 guests, there may be more as we still have 9 months but even if we don&#039;t I am so happy and excited! &amp;nbsp;Thanks for the *hugs* :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"Sarahop81\"] I&#039;m so sorry to hear that babe, it&#039;s so unfair for you. &amp;nbsp;But you are right, focus on you and your soon-to-be husband and that&#039;s all you need. &amp;nbsp;I am not chasing people anymore, I sent some friendly reminder texts &amp;amp; emails and now that&#039;s it. &amp;nbsp;You come or you don&#039;t. &amp;nbsp;I have the important people there and 32 people have already committed. &amp;nbsp;That is more than I could every ask for. &amp;nbsp;And most importantly, I get to marry the man of my dreams :) &amp;nbsp;I hope it all works out for you!!! &amp;nbsp;When is your big day?&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I contemplated having some sort of after party or gathering for my family and friends in Canada that couldn&#039;t make it but their lack of response and general attitude makes me not want to. &amp;nbsp;Why should I go out of my way to plan something that is primarily for them when they can&#039;t be bother to rsvp, who&#039;s to say they would even come to that.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1900666,"PostDate":1437147556,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a> Thank you <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0That killed me too when she said she thought I would get a free trip. \u00a0The nerve! \u00a0I actually read back our conversation because I'm so rattled and realized when she said about having to pay by october she actually said \"why do we have to pay by October, the TRIP isn't until April\" \u00a0TRIP! \u00a0She called it a trip and not my wedding. \u00a0Maybe I'm reading too much into it and she didn't mean it that way, but after the convo we had I really think she did. \u00a0I'm 100% going to focus on our 32 guests, there may be more as we still have 9 months but even if we don't I am so happy and excited! \u00a0Thanks for the *hugs* <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"276722\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/276722-sarahop81\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Sarahop81<\/span><\/a> I'm so sorry to hear that babe, it's so unfair for you. \u00a0But you are right, focus on you and your soon-to-be husband and that's all you need. \u00a0I am not chasing people anymore, I sent some friendly reminder texts & emails and now that's it. \u00a0You come or you don't. \u00a0I have the important people there and 32 people have already committed. \u00a0That is more than I could every ask for. \u00a0And most importantly, I get to marry the man of my dreams <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0I hope it all works out for you!!! \u00a0When is your big day?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I contemplated having some sort of after party or gathering for my family and friends in Canada that couldn't make it but their lack of response and general attitude makes me not want to. \u00a0Why should I go out of my way to plan something that is primarily for them when they can't be bother to rsvp, who's to say they would even come to that.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><img src=\"http:\/\/\" alt=\"\"><\/div>\n<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;0\/st\/20160423\/e\/we+leave+for+Mexico%21\/k\/c059\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;32;116\/st\/20160430\/e\/we+say+I+do%21\/k\/8afc\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529<\/a>","Email":"deannaproteau@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1421424569,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1443808962","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"deecol","Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"68.146.146.173","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79405,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7f8196823a7a09a83a6adcb77f3d9de4","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"deecol\"]&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I am probably not the one for advice on your last mention of the AHR. &amp;nbsp;I tend to be one who can hold a grudge and I would probably do that just out of spite. &amp;nbsp;That said, I didn&#039;t have an AHR, honestly never even considered it. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Shawn had mentioned it once for his family back in ON -- he has a GINORMOUS family and there was just no way we could invite them all, but one day we will make it there so I can meet them! &amp;nbsp;   &lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I tend to agree with your logic though. &amp;nbsp;Why have a party so they can celebrate you when they didn&#039;t even have the decency to RSVP or reply to your msgs\/texts. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;But once the frustration has worn off you will see it with new eyes and that&#039;s probably the better time to make the decision :) &amp;nbsp;Good luck!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1900668,"PostDate":1437147789,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281751\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281751-deecol\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">deecol<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>I am probably not the one for advice on your last mention of the AHR. \u00a0I tend to be one who can hold a grudge and I would probably do that just out of spite. \u00a0That said, I didn't have an AHR, honestly never even considered it. \u00a0 \u00a0Shawn had mentioned it once for his family back in ON -- he has a GINORMOUS family and there was just no way we could invite them all, but one day we will make it there so I can meet them! \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I tend to agree with your logic though. \u00a0Why have a party so they can celebrate you when they didn't even have the decency to RSVP or reply to your msgs\/texts. \u00a0 \u00a0But once the frustration has worn off you will see it with new eyes and that's probably the better time to make the decision <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0Good luck!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399410602,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"200.79.251.123","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79405,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":6,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f6b6314c4714d85dd9e0036878049896","RawContent":"[quote name=\"deecol\" post=\"1900645\" timestamp=\"1437147160\"]\nHi Ladies!\n\nI really need to vent, and if anyone will understand it will be you.\n\nI don&#039;t even have to say this, we all know that when it comes to destination weddings, some people will be there and book without hesitation, some will say yes and not book, and some will not be able to attend.  What I&#039;m finding extremely difficult to process and understand is the complete lack of communication and respect my own family and \"close\" friends have for me and my fianc\u00e9.\n\nWe get a group rate and reserve seats, give months of advance warning and in every reminder email I have sent I have expressed that they are more than welcome to make their own accommodations, however they may not get the same price or the hotel may not have room for them when they do decide to book.\n\nMy booking deadline is next week.  I have 6 people who have guaranteed me they will book by this date.  One of my friends texted me to let me know she&#039;s booking on Saturday, she obviously didn&#039;t read the last email I sent where I let everyone know the agency is closed on weekends, it&#039;s no problem, she can call Monday, but then I thought, shoot - maybe I should let the others know.  So I text one of my \"close\" girlfriends, she then asks me \"do we have to pay by October? because I can&#039;t\".  No problem, you don&#039;t have to but there is a early booking bonus included in my rate and you will have to pay that if you miss the deadline and told her to feel free to look into other options.  She then says \"Your wedding is in April LOL, I don&#039;t get why we have to pay so early, I travel to resorts quite a bit and they&#039;re never sold out in April\".  Trying not to be rude I let her know that I am not psychic and have no way of knowing if the price will go up or down, and if the resort will sell out or not, all I did was negotiate a group rate and reserved some seats so my closest family and friends can hold their spot.  My fianc\u00e9 has worked in travel all his life, we did a lot of research before choosing this resort and date.  The final straw of this conversation:  I tell her, I get it, it is an expense and Colin and I need to have our payment in by October too.  She says: Oh, you guys have to pay?  I just thought you were trying to get a certain amount of people to book so you could get a free trip.  It made me feel like I&#039;m being perceived as a scammer and I should not feel like this when I&#039;m trying to plan my wedding.  Yes, sometimes we get incentives on trips if a certain number of people book, but if she was such a close friend she would have talked to me about how my wedding plans are going so far and realized I am no where near even getting one comp ticket.  It doesn&#039;t matter to me, we are getting married, it&#039;s an expense, a comp would be a bonus but that&#039;s not the reason I arranged a group rate.  I let her know that when we looked at this resort for 2015 a couple weeks before our dates it was sold out so she can take her chances, we ended the conversation by her patronizing me \"Oh really?  I&#039;ve never seen that, must have been spring breakers. Woooo\"  And we agreed for her to look into other options.  I&#039;m at the point right now where I don&#039;t care.  Do what you want.\n\nThe other shocker in my current situation is my Dad&#039;s side of the family.  He has 5 siblings, they all have kids and some of them have kids.  I have always been close with them, they know my dad and I have always had a great relationship especially through my parents divorce and we have always stayed in contact.  My Dad will be the only one from his side at my wedding.  I understand not being able to afford it, and that is completely okay, but when my cousin got married in Nova Scotia, they all went.  Another just got engaged that lives there and I&#039;m sure they will all go.  Some are even going down this summer.  When I was trying to collect their addresses for my invites it was so difficult, then I send the invitations and I don&#039;t even get a reply, nothing to even say they can&#039;t make it.  This really upsets my Dad, so he who is scared to even use a computer posted a FACEBOOK message to his family.  No one responded.  So now he&#039;s calling everyone individually, and as the declines roll in, I&#039;m not upset, I&#039;m upset with those family members who my dad has spoken to and they still haven&#039;t contacted me, and those family members who he is chasing down, he shouldn&#039;t have to chase them down.  He had planned to share a room with one of my cousins, my cousin has ignored every phone call from him, every message from me, but told other family members that he can&#039;t commit right now and will probably book later.  Why couldn&#039;t he tell one of us that?  My dad was left to find someone to share a room with and luckily a friend of mine from elementary school needed a room-mate.  It makes my Dad really upset, which is not fair to him.\n\nTrying not to let it bother me and focus on the fact that we have 32 of our closest family and friends from Canada and the UK with their deposits down.  That is more than I could ever ask for.\n\nThanks for letting me rant :)[\/quote][quote name=\"deecol\" post=\"1900645\" timestamp=\"1437147160\"]\nHi Ladies!\n\nI really need to vent, and if anyone will understand it will be you.\n\nI don&#039;t even have to say this, we all know that when it comes to destination weddings, some people will be there and book without hesitation, some will say yes and not book, and some will not be able to attend.  What I&#039;m finding extremely difficult to process and understand is the complete lack of communication and respect my own family and \"close\" friends have for me and my fianc\u00e9.\n\nWe get a group rate and reserve seats, give months of advance warning and in every reminder email I have sent I have expressed that they are more than welcome to make their own accommodations, however they may not get the same price or the hotel may not have room for them when they do decide to book.\n\nMy booking deadline is next week.  I have 6 people who have guaranteed me they will book by this date.  One of my friends texted me to let me know she&#039;s booking on Saturday, she obviously didn&#039;t read the last email I sent where I let everyone know the agency is closed on weekends, it&#039;s no problem, she can call Monday, but then I thought, shoot - maybe I should let the others know.  So I text one of my \"close\" girlfriends, she then asks me \"do we have to pay by October? because I can&#039;t\".  No problem, you don&#039;t have to but there is a early booking bonus included in my rate and you will have to pay that if you miss the deadline and told her to feel free to look into other options.  She then says \"Your wedding is in April LOL, I don&#039;t get why we have to pay so early, I travel to resorts quite a bit and they&#039;re never sold out in April\".  Trying not to be rude I let her know that I am not psychic and have no way of knowing if the price will go up or down, and if the resort will sell out or not, all I did was negotiate a group rate and reserved some seats so my closest family and friends can hold their spot.  My fianc\u00e9 has worked in travel all his life, we did a lot of research before choosing this resort and date.  The final straw of this conversation:  I tell her, I get it, it is an expense and Colin and I need to have our payment in by October too.  She says: Oh, you guys have to pay?  I just thought you were trying to get a certain amount of people to book so you could get a free trip.  It made me feel like I&#039;m being perceived as a scammer and I should not feel like this when I&#039;m trying to plan my wedding.  Yes, sometimes we get incentives on trips if a certain number of people book, but if she was such a close friend she would have talked to me about how my wedding plans are going so far and realized I am no where near even getting one comp ticket.  It doesn&#039;t matter to me, we are getting married, it&#039;s an expense, a comp would be a bonus but that&#039;s not the reason I arranged a group rate.  I let her know that when we looked at this resort for 2015 a couple weeks before our dates it was sold out so she can take her chances, we ended the conversation by her patronizing me \"Oh really?  I&#039;ve never seen that, must have been spring breakers. Woooo\"  And we agreed for her to look into other options.  I&#039;m at the point right now where I don&#039;t care.  Do what you want.\n\nThe other shocker in my current situation is my Dad&#039;s side of the family.  He has 5 siblings, they all have kids and some of them have kids.  I have always been close with them, they know my dad and I have always had a great relationship especially through my parents divorce and we have always stayed in contact.  My Dad will be the only one from his side at my wedding.  I understand not being able to afford it, and that is completely okay, but when my cousin got married in Nova Scotia, they all went.  Another just got engaged that lives there and I&#039;m sure they will all go.  Some are even going down this summer.  When I was trying to collect their addresses for my invites it was so difficult, then I send the invitations and I don&#039;t even get a reply, nothing to even say they can&#039;t make it.  This really upsets my Dad, so he who is scared to even use a computer posted a FACEBOOK message to his family.  No one responded.  So now he&#039;s calling everyone individually, and as the declines roll in, I&#039;m not upset, I&#039;m upset with those family members who my dad has spoken to and they still haven&#039;t contacted me, and those family members who he is chasing down, he shouldn&#039;t have to chase them down.  He had planned to share a room with one of my cousins, my cousin has ignored every phone call from him, every message from me, but told other family members that he can&#039;t commit right now and will probably book later.  Why couldn&#039;t he tell one of us that?  My dad was left to find someone to share a room with and luckily a friend of mine from elementary school needed a room-mate.  It makes my Dad really upset, which is not fair to him.\n\nTrying not to let it bother me and focus on the fact that we have 32 of our closest family and friends from Canada and the UK with their deposits down.  That is more than I could ever ask for.\n\nThanks for letting me rant :)[\/quote][quote name=\"deecol\" post=\"1900645\" timestamp=\"1437147160\"]\nHi Ladies!\n\nI really need to vent, and if anyone will understand it will be you.\n\nI don&#039;t even have to say this, we all know that when it comes to destination weddings, some people will be there and book without hesitation, some will say yes and not book, and some will not be able to attend.  What I&#039;m finding extremely difficult to process and understand is the complete lack of communication and respect my own family and \"close\" friends have for me and my fianc\u00e9.\n\nWe get a group rate and reserve seats, give months of advance warning and in every reminder email I have sent I have expressed that they are more than welcome to make their own accommodations, however they may not get the same price or the hotel may not have room for them when they do decide to book.\n\nMy booking deadline is next week.  I have 6 people who have guaranteed me they will book by this date.  One of my friends texted me to let me know she&#039;s booking on Saturday, she obviously didn&#039;t read the last email I sent where I let everyone know the agency is closed on weekends, it&#039;s no problem, she can call Monday, but then I thought, shoot - maybe I should let the others know.  So I text one of my \"close\" girlfriends, she then asks me \"do we have to pay by October? because I can&#039;t\".  No problem, you don&#039;t have to but there is a early booking bonus included in my rate and you will have to pay that if you miss the deadline and told her to feel free to look into other options.  She then says \"Your wedding is in April LOL, I don&#039;t get why we have to pay so early, I travel to resorts quite a bit and they&#039;re never sold out in April\".  Trying not to be rude I let her know that I am not psychic and have no way of knowing if the price will go up or down, and if the resort will sell out or not, all I did was negotiate a group rate and reserved some seats so my closest family and friends can hold their spot.  My fianc\u00e9 has worked in travel all his life, we did a lot of research before choosing this resort and date.  The final straw of this conversation:  I tell her, I get it, it is an expense and Colin and I need to have our payment in by October too.  She says: Oh, you guys have to pay?  I just thought you were trying to get a certain amount of people to book so you could get a free trip.  It made me feel like I&#039;m being perceived as a scammer and I should not feel like this when I&#039;m trying to plan my wedding.  Yes, sometimes we get incentives on trips if a certain number of people book, but if she was such a close friend she would have talked to me about how my wedding plans are going so far and realized I am no where near even getting one comp ticket.  It doesn&#039;t matter to me, we are getting married, it&#039;s an expense, a comp would be a bonus but that&#039;s not the reason I arranged a group rate.  I let her know that when we looked at this resort for 2015 a couple weeks before our dates it was sold out so she can take her chances, we ended the conversation by her patronizing me \"Oh really?  I&#039;ve never seen that, must have been spring breakers. Woooo\"  And we agreed for her to look into other options.  I&#039;m at the point right now where I don&#039;t care.  Do what you want.\n\nThe other shocker in my current situation is my Dad&#039;s side of the family.  He has 5 siblings, they all have kids and some of them have kids.  I have always been close with them, they know my dad and I have always had a great relationship especially through my parents divorce and we have always stayed in contact.  My Dad will be the only one from his side at my wedding.  I understand not being able to afford it, and that is completely okay, but when my cousin got married in Nova Scotia, they all went.  Another just got engaged that lives there and I&#039;m sure they will all go.  Some are even going down this summer.  When I was trying to collect their addresses for my invites it was so difficult, then I send the invitations and I don&#039;t even get a reply, nothing to even say they can&#039;t make it.  This really upsets my Dad, so he who is scared to even use a computer posted a FACEBOOK message to his family.  No one responded.  So now he&#039;s calling everyone individually, and as the declines roll in, I&#039;m not upset, I&#039;m upset with those family members who my dad has spoken to and they still haven&#039;t contacted me, and those family members who he is chasing down, he shouldn&#039;t have to chase them down.  He had planned to share a room with one of my cousins, my cousin has ignored every phone call from him, every message from me, but told other family members that he can&#039;t commit right now and will probably book later.  Why couldn&#039;t he tell one of us that?  My dad was left to find someone to share a room with and luckily a friend of mine from elementary school needed a room-mate.  It makes my Dad really upset, which is not fair to him.\n\nTrying not to let it bother me and focus on the fact that we have 32 of our closest family and friends from Canada and the UK with their deposits down.  That is more than I could ever ask for.\n\nThanks for letting me rant :)[\/quote]Hey Deecol,\n\nFirst of big big hugs to you... I see this happens quite often with destination wedding.   Great advice from the other ladies as well.   \n\nMy advice I give to all brides to be:\n\n1.  Important people will be there not matter what.\n2.  Consider yourself fortunate you already have 32 guests booked\n3.  Your friend may not know how to tell you, no she cant make it, only coming u with some insane excuses.\n4.  About your AHR, I would wait until the wedding planning stages is done , then make the decision.\n5.  You have done your part, sent reminders , calls etc.  NOW enjoy planning your wedding.\n6.  This is about You and your fiancee, let the people who want to hop on the train enjoy the ride, and those who are n\u00b4t            taking action leave them behind. it will be their loss not yours.\n\nHappy Planning and Im sure you will have a beautiful wedding.  \nJoyce","Attachments":[],"Id":1900673,"PostDate":1437153603,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>deecol, on 17 July 2015 - 10:32 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Hi Ladies!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I really need to vent, and if anyone will understand it will be you.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I don't even have to say this, we all know that when it comes to destination weddings, some people will be there and book without hesitation, some will say yes and not book, and some will not be able to attend. \u00a0What I'm finding extremely difficult to process and understand is the complete lack of communication and respect my own family and \"close\" friends have for me and my fianc\u00e9.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We get a group rate and reserve seats, give months of advance warning and in every reminder email I have sent I have expressed that they are more than welcome to make their own accommodations, however they may not get the same price or the hotel may not have room for them when they do decide to book.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My booking deadline is next week. \u00a0I have 6 people who have guaranteed me they will book by this date. \u00a0One of my friends texted me to let me know she's booking on Saturday, she obviously didn't read the last email I sent where I let everyone know the agency is closed on weekends, it's no problem, she can call Monday, but then I thought, shoot - maybe I should let the others know. \u00a0So I text one of my \"close\" girlfriends, she then asks me \"do we have to pay by October? because I can't\". \u00a0No problem, you don't have to but there is a early booking bonus included in my rate and you will have to pay that if you miss the deadline and told her to feel free to look into other options. \u00a0She then says \"Your wedding is in April LOL, I don't get why we have to pay so early, I travel to resorts quite a bit and they're never sold out in April\". \u00a0Trying not to be rude I let her know that I am not psychic and have no way of knowing if the price will go up or down, and if the resort will sell out or not, all I did was negotiate a group rate and reserved some seats so my closest family and friends can hold their spot. \u00a0My fianc\u00e9 has worked in travel all his life, we did a lot of research before choosing this resort and date. \u00a0The final straw of this conversation: \u00a0I tell her, I get it, it is an expense and Colin and I need to have our payment in by October too. \u00a0She says: Oh, you guys have to pay? \u00a0I just thought you were trying to get a certain amount of people to book so you could get a free trip. \u00a0It made me feel like I'm being perceived as a scammer and I should not feel like this when I'm trying to plan my wedding. \u00a0Yes, sometimes we get incentives on trips if a certain number of people book, but if she was such a close friend she would have talked to me about how my wedding plans are going so far and realized I am no where near even getting one comp ticket. \u00a0It doesn't matter to me, we are getting married, it's an expense, a comp would be a bonus but that's not the reason I arranged a group rate. \u00a0I let her know that when we looked at this resort for 2015 a couple weeks before our dates it was sold out so she can take her chances, we ended the conversation by her patronizing me \"Oh really? \u00a0I've never seen that, must have been spring breakers. Woooo\" \u00a0And we agreed for her to look into other options. \u00a0I'm at the point right now where I don't care. \u00a0Do what you want.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The other shocker in my current situation is my Dad's side of the family. \u00a0He has 5 siblings, they all have kids and some of them have kids. \u00a0I have always been close with them, they know my dad and I have always had a great relationship especially through my parents divorce and we have always stayed in contact. \u00a0My Dad will be the only one from his side at my wedding. \u00a0I understand not being able to afford it, and that is completely okay, but when my cousin got married in Nova Scotia, they all went. \u00a0Another just got engaged that lives there and I'm sure they will all go. \u00a0Some are even going down this summer. \u00a0When I was trying to collect their addresses for my invites it was so difficult, then I send the invitations and I don't even get a reply, nothing to even say they can't make it. \u00a0This really upsets my Dad, so he who is scared to even use a computer posted a FACEBOOK message to his family. \u00a0No one responded. \u00a0So now he's calling everyone individually, and as the declines roll in, I'm not upset, I'm upset with those family members who my dad has spoken to and they still haven't contacted me, and those family members who he is chasing down, he shouldn't have to chase them down. \u00a0He had planned to share a room with one of my cousins, my cousin has ignored every phone call from him, every message from me, but told other family members that he can't commit right now and will probably book later. \u00a0Why couldn't he tell one of us that? \u00a0My dad was left to find someone to share a room with and luckily a friend of mine from elementary school needed a room-mate. \u00a0It makes my Dad really upset, which is not fair to him.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Trying not to let it bother me and focus on the fact that we have 32 of our closest family and friends from Canada and the UK with their deposits down. \u00a0That is more than I could ever ask for.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Thanks for letting me rant <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>deecol, on 17 July 2015 - 10:32 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Hi Ladies!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I really need to vent, and if anyone will understand it will be you.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I don't even have to say this, we all know that when it comes to destination weddings, some people will be there and book without hesitation, some will say yes and not book, and some will not be able to attend. \u00a0What I'm finding extremely difficult to process and understand is the complete lack of communication and respect my own family and \"close\" friends have for me and my fianc\u00e9.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We get a group rate and reserve seats, give months of advance warning and in every reminder email I have sent I have expressed that they are more than welcome to make their own accommodations, however they may not get the same price or the hotel may not have room for them when they do decide to book.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My booking deadline is next week. \u00a0I have 6 people who have guaranteed me they will book by this date. \u00a0One of my friends texted me to let me know she's booking on Saturday, she obviously didn't read the last email I sent where I let everyone know the agency is closed on weekends, it's no problem, she can call Monday, but then I thought, shoot - maybe I should let the others know. \u00a0So I text one of my \"close\" girlfriends, she then asks me \"do we have to pay by October? because I can't\". \u00a0No problem, you don't have to but there is a early booking bonus included in my rate and you will have to pay that if you miss the deadline and told her to feel free to look into other options. \u00a0She then says \"Your wedding is in April LOL, I don't get why we have to pay so early, I travel to resorts quite a bit and they're never sold out in April\". \u00a0Trying not to be rude I let her know that I am not psychic and have no way of knowing if the price will go up or down, and if the resort will sell out or not, all I did was negotiate a group rate and reserved some seats so my closest family and friends can hold their spot. \u00a0My fianc\u00e9 has worked in travel all his life, we did a lot of research before choosing this resort and date. \u00a0The final straw of this conversation: \u00a0I tell her, I get it, it is an expense and Colin and I need to have our payment in by October too. \u00a0She says: Oh, you guys have to pay? \u00a0I just thought you were trying to get a certain amount of people to book so you could get a free trip. \u00a0It made me feel like I'm being perceived as a scammer and I should not feel like this when I'm trying to plan my wedding. \u00a0Yes, sometimes we get incentives on trips if a certain number of people book, but if she was such a close friend she would have talked to me about how my wedding plans are going so far and realized I am no where near even getting one comp ticket. \u00a0It doesn't matter to me, we are getting married, it's an expense, a comp would be a bonus but that's not the reason I arranged a group rate. \u00a0I let her know that when we looked at this resort for 2015 a couple weeks before our dates it was sold out so she can take her chances, we ended the conversation by her patronizing me \"Oh really? \u00a0I've never seen that, must have been spring breakers. Woooo\" \u00a0And we agreed for her to look into other options. \u00a0I'm at the point right now where I don't care. \u00a0Do what you want.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The other shocker in my current situation is my Dad's side of the family. \u00a0He has 5 siblings, they all have kids and some of them have kids. \u00a0I have always been close with them, they know my dad and I have always had a great relationship especially through my parents divorce and we have always stayed in contact. \u00a0My Dad will be the only one from his side at my wedding. \u00a0I understand not being able to afford it, and that is completely okay, but when my cousin got married in Nova Scotia, they all went. \u00a0Another just got engaged that lives there and I'm sure they will all go. \u00a0Some are even going down this summer. \u00a0When I was trying to collect their addresses for my invites it was so difficult, then I send the invitations and I don't even get a reply, nothing to even say they can't make it. \u00a0This really upsets my Dad, so he who is scared to even use a computer posted a FACEBOOK message to his family. \u00a0No one responded. \u00a0So now he's calling everyone individually, and as the declines roll in, I'm not upset, I'm upset with those family members who my dad has spoken to and they still haven't contacted me, and those family members who he is chasing down, he shouldn't have to chase them down. \u00a0He had planned to share a room with one of my cousins, my cousin has ignored every phone call from him, every message from me, but told other family members that he can't commit right now and will probably book later. \u00a0Why couldn't he tell one of us that? \u00a0My dad was left to find someone to share a room with and luckily a friend of mine from elementary school needed a room-mate. \u00a0It makes my Dad really upset, which is not fair to him.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Trying not to let it bother me and focus on the fact that we have 32 of our closest family and friends from Canada and the UK with their deposits down. \u00a0That is more than I could ever ask for.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Thanks for letting me rant <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>deecol, on 17 July 2015 - 10:32 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Hi Ladies!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I really need to vent, and if anyone will understand it will be you.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I don't even have to say this, we all know that when it comes to destination weddings, some people will be there and book without hesitation, some will say yes and not book, and some will not be able to attend. \u00a0What I'm finding extremely difficult to process and understand is the complete lack of communication and respect my own family and \"close\" friends have for me and my fianc\u00e9.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We get a group rate and reserve seats, give months of advance warning and in every reminder email I have sent I have expressed that they are more than welcome to make their own accommodations, however they may not get the same price or the hotel may not have room for them when they do decide to book.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My booking deadline is next week. \u00a0I have 6 people who have guaranteed me they will book by this date. \u00a0One of my friends texted me to let me know she's booking on Saturday, she obviously didn't read the last email I sent where I let everyone know the agency is closed on weekends, it's no problem, she can call Monday, but then I thought, shoot - maybe I should let the others know. \u00a0So I text one of my \"close\" girlfriends, she then asks me \"do we have to pay by October? because I can't\". \u00a0No problem, you don't have to but there is a early booking bonus included in my rate and you will have to pay that if you miss the deadline and told her to feel free to look into other options. \u00a0She then says \"Your wedding is in April LOL, I don't get why we have to pay so early, I travel to resorts quite a bit and they're never sold out in April\". \u00a0Trying not to be rude I let her know that I am not psychic and have no way of knowing if the price will go up or down, and if the resort will sell out or not, all I did was negotiate a group rate and reserved some seats so my closest family and friends can hold their spot. \u00a0My fianc\u00e9 has worked in travel all his life, we did a lot of research before choosing this resort and date. \u00a0The final straw of this conversation: \u00a0I tell her, I get it, it is an expense and Colin and I need to have our payment in by October too. \u00a0She says: Oh, you guys have to pay? \u00a0I just thought you were trying to get a certain amount of people to book so you could get a free trip. \u00a0It made me feel like I'm being perceived as a scammer and I should not feel like this when I'm trying to plan my wedding. \u00a0Yes, sometimes we get incentives on trips if a certain number of people book, but if she was such a close friend she would have talked to me about how my wedding plans are going so far and realized I am no where near even getting one comp ticket. \u00a0It doesn't matter to me, we are getting married, it's an expense, a comp would be a bonus but that's not the reason I arranged a group rate. \u00a0I let her know that when we looked at this resort for 2015 a couple weeks before our dates it was sold out so she can take her chances, we ended the conversation by her patronizing me \"Oh really? \u00a0I've never seen that, must have been spring breakers. Woooo\" \u00a0And we agreed for her to look into other options. \u00a0I'm at the point right now where I don't care. \u00a0Do what you want.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The other shocker in my current situation is my Dad's side of the family. \u00a0He has 5 siblings, they all have kids and some of them have kids. \u00a0I have always been close with them, they know my dad and I have always had a great relationship especially through my parents divorce and we have always stayed in contact. \u00a0My Dad will be the only one from his side at my wedding. \u00a0I understand not being able to afford it, and that is completely okay, but when my cousin got married in Nova Scotia, they all went. \u00a0Another just got engaged that lives there and I'm sure they will all go. \u00a0Some are even going down this summer. \u00a0When I was trying to collect their addresses for my invites it was so difficult, then I send the invitations and I don't even get a reply, nothing to even say they can't make it. \u00a0This really upsets my Dad, so he who is scared to even use a computer posted a FACEBOOK message to his family. \u00a0No one responded. \u00a0So now he's calling everyone individually, and as the declines roll in, I'm not upset, I'm upset with those family members who my dad has spoken to and they still haven't contacted me, and those family members who he is chasing down, he shouldn't have to chase them down. \u00a0He had planned to share a room with one of my cousins, my cousin has ignored every phone call from him, every message from me, but told other family members that he can't commit right now and will probably book later. \u00a0Why couldn't he tell one of us that? \u00a0My dad was left to find someone to share a room with and luckily a friend of mine from elementary school needed a room-mate. \u00a0It makes my Dad really upset, which is not fair to him.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Trying not to let it bother me and focus on the fact that we have 32 of our closest family and friends from Canada and the UK with their deposits down. \u00a0That is more than I could ever ask for.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Thanks for letting me rant <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>Hey Deecol,<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>First of big big hugs to you... I see this happens quite often with destination wedding. \u00a0 Great advice from the other ladies as well. \u00a0\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My advice I give to all brides to be:<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>1. \u00a0Important people will be there not matter what.<\/p>\n<p>2. \u00a0Consider yourself fortunate you already have 32 guests booked<\/p>\n<p>3. \u00a0Your friend may not know how to tell you, no she cant make it, only coming u with some insane excuses.<\/p>\n<p>4. \u00a0About your AHR, I would wait until the wedding planning stages is done , then make the decision.<\/p>\n<p>5. \u00a0You have done your part, sent reminders , calls etc. \u00a0NOW enjoy planning your wedding.<\/p>\n<p>6. \u00a0This is about You and your fiancee, let the people who want to hop on the train enjoy the ride, and those who are n\u00b4t \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0taking action leave them behind. it will be their loss not yours.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Happy Planning and Im sure you will have a beautiful wedding. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Joyce<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"Dream Weddings Riviera Maya- We pay attention to your wishes and coordinate closely with you to ensure your wedding or event is planned to perfection!<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<span style='color: rgb(40,40,40)'><span style='font-family: arial'><span style='font-size: 12px;'>Dream Weddings Riviera Maya<\/span><\/span><\/span><br \/>\n<span style='font-family: arial'><span style='font-size: 12px;'>weddingsinplayadelcarmen@gmail.com<\/span><\/span><br \/>\n<a class='bbc_url' href='http:\/\/www.dreamweddingsrivieramaya.com\/Home_Page.html'>http:\/\/www.dreamweddingsrivieramaya.com\/Home_Page.html<\/a><br \/>\n<br \/>\n<span style='color: rgb(40,40,40)'><span style='font-family: arial'><span style='font-size: 12px;'>Happy Planning!<\/span><\/span><\/span><br \/>\n<span style='color: rgb(40,40,40)'><span style='font-family: arial'><span style='font-size: 12px;'>Joyce<\/span><\/span><\/span>","Email":"weddingsinplayadelcarmen@gmail.com","IpAddress":"187.252.44.28","GroupId":84,"GroupName":"Insiders w\/ Articles","JoinDate":1326836387,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-250090.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"dreamweddings","Id":250090,"Name":"dreamweddings","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"99.233.132.193","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79405,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":3,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"79936ee42e76da2a94ea8622a60ab8f3","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"dreamweddings\"] Thank you Joyce! &amp;nbsp;You&#039;re tips made me smile. &amp;nbsp;In the end it is definitely about me and my fianc\u00e9 and I&#039;m so thankful to those that have already committed to coming.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Venting on this forum and all the kind words have already made me start feeling better about the whole thing.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Thanks again :) xo&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1900683,"PostDate":1437166951,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"250090\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/250090-dreamweddings\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">dreamweddings<\/span><\/a> Thank you Joyce! \u00a0You're tips made me smile. \u00a0In the end it is definitely about me and my fianc\u00e9 and I'm so thankful to those that have already committed to coming.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Venting on this forum and all the kind words have already made me start feeling better about the whole thing.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Thanks again <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> xo\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><img src=\"http:\/\/\" alt=\"\"><\/div>\n<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;0\/st\/20160423\/e\/we+leave+for+Mexico%21\/k\/c059\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;32;116\/st\/20160430\/e\/we+say+I+do%21\/k\/8afc\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529<\/a>","Email":"deannaproteau@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1421424569,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1443808962","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"deecol","Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.212.156.114","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79405,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1437252320,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c14ef5033cfa6bf9b21bc6aa223146d0","RawContent":"I feel so badly for all of you. We went through the same thing when we got married almost 4 years ago and actually ended up going just the two of us. Not fun Yes. But it came down to what&#039;s important and in the end it was the two of us getting married on the beach in Jamaica. Whoever is travelling with you, love them even more for going. The ones that aren&#039;t let it go and don&#039;t let it ruin anything for you.  Nothing brings out the worst in families like weddings and funerals!! Best of luck.  Your wedding will be fabulous!!\n\n\nSent from my SGH-I337M using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1900686,"PostDate":1437168995,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I feel so badly for all of you. We went through the same thing when we got married almost 4 years ago and actually ended up going just the two of us. Not fun Yes. But it came down to what's important and in the end it was the two of us getting married on the beach in Jamaica. Whoever is travelling with you, love them even more for going. The ones that aren't let it go and don't let it ruin anything for you.  Nothing brings out the worst in families like weddings and funerals!! Best of luck.  Your wedding will be fabulous!!<br><br>\nSent from my SGH-I337M using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><span style=\"color:#ff0099;\"><em>I said \"yes\" again to the love of my life at Grand Coral Beach Club, Playa del Carmen, Mexico on our 4th anniversary - October 20, 2015<\/em><\/span>","Email":"achadwick9@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"206.223.185.220","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1283440999,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1434318164","PhotoWidth":570,"PhotoHeight":541,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"acw271011","Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79405,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7506dbbbbe68013c5ea6e2956a341d94","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Update: &amp;nbsp;My girlfriend messages me the day after the booking deadline \"Sorry! &amp;nbsp;I forgot to call the travel agent, I&#039;ve been so sick the past two days\"... Then posts a picture of herself with a glass of wine on instagram 5 hours after messaging me. &amp;nbsp;I thought that was too funny not to share. &amp;nbsp;Haven&#039;t had much communication since, it&#039;s up to her if she wants to come. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m not stressing. &amp;nbsp;We had a couple more people book since and I couldn&#039;t be happier :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;My Dad&#039;s family have started responding. &amp;nbsp;Mostly declines but at least it&#039;s a response. &amp;nbsp;And I found out through the travel agent that 2 of them have been in contact with her, they still haven&#039;t said anything to me but good to know they&#039;re considering. &amp;nbsp;My TA extended the deadline by another 2 weeks so they may book. &amp;nbsp;Again, if they don&#039;t, I&#039;m still super happy and excited!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1901236,"PostDate":1437990415,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Update: \u00a0My girlfriend messages me the day after the booking deadline \"Sorry! \u00a0I forgot to call the travel agent, I've been so sick the past two days\"... Then posts a picture of herself with a glass of wine on instagram 5 hours after messaging me. \u00a0I thought that was too funny not to share. \u00a0Haven't had much communication since, it's up to her if she wants to come. \u00a0I'm not stressing. \u00a0We had a couple more people book since and I couldn't be happier <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Dad's family have started responding. \u00a0Mostly declines but at least it's a response. \u00a0And I found out through the travel agent that 2 of them have been in contact with her, they still haven't said anything to me but good to know they're considering. \u00a0My TA extended the deadline by another 2 weeks so they may book. \u00a0Again, if they don't, I'm still super happy and excited!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><img src=\"http:\/\/\" alt=\"\"><\/div>\n<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;0\/st\/20160423\/e\/we+leave+for+Mexico%21\/k\/c059\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;32;116\/st\/20160430\/e\/we+say+I+do%21\/k\/8afc\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529<\/a>","Email":"deannaproteau@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1421424569,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1443808962","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"deecol","Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"68.146.146.173","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79405,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c8eee06d3a6c25c15a2c0dadd806944b","RawContent":"[quote name=\"deecol\" post=\"1901236\" timestamp=\"1438008415\"]\nUpdate:  My girlfriend messages me the day after the booking deadline \"Sorry!  I forgot to call the travel agent, I&#039;ve been so sick the past two days\"... Then posts a picture of herself with a glass of wine on instagram 5 hours after messaging me.  I thought that was too funny not to share.  Haven&#039;t had much communication since, it&#039;s up to her if she wants to come.  I&#039;m not stressing.  We had a couple more people book since and I couldn&#039;t be happier :)\n\nMy Dad&#039;s family have started responding.  Mostly declines but at least it&#039;s a response.  And I found out through the travel agent that 2 of them have been in contact with her, they still haven&#039;t said anything to me but good to know they&#039;re considering.  My TA extended the deadline by another 2 weeks so they may book.  Again, if they don&#039;t, I&#039;m still super happy and excited![\/quote]\nPeople!  I find this quite common actually.  Not sure if people forget social media makes things public or they don&#039;t care LOL!!   Shawn&#039;s cousin was going to do our engagement photos, we had the day set up, etc.  She called to cancel saying she had to work but then posted pics all day on FB of her trip to Banff.    Shawn was already uneasy about her but this put him over the edge. We haven&#039;t talked to her since LOL....   \n\nHopefully in the next 2 weeks you get your final headcount.","Attachments":[],"Id":1901310,"PostDate":1438072405,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>deecol, on 27 July 2015 - 09:46 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Update: \u00a0My girlfriend messages me the day after the booking deadline \"Sorry! \u00a0I forgot to call the travel agent, I've been so sick the past two days\"... Then posts a picture of herself with a glass of wine on instagram 5 hours after messaging me. \u00a0I thought that was too funny not to share. \u00a0Haven't had much communication since, it's up to her if she wants to come. \u00a0I'm not stressing. \u00a0We had a couple more people book since and I couldn't be happier <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Dad's family have started responding. \u00a0Mostly declines but at least it's a response. \u00a0And I found out through the travel agent that 2 of them have been in contact with her, they still haven't said anything to me but good to know they're considering. \u00a0My TA extended the deadline by another 2 weeks so they may book. \u00a0Again, if they don't, I'm still super happy and excited!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>People! \u00a0I find this quite common actually. \u00a0Not sure if people forget social media makes things public or they don't care LOL!! \u00a0 Shawn's cousin was going to do our engagement photos, we had the day set up, etc. \u00a0She called to cancel saying she had to work but then posted pics all day on FB of her trip to Banff. \u00a0 \u00a0Shawn was already uneasy about her but this put him over the edge. We haven't talked to her since LOL.... \u00a0\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Hopefully in the next 2 weeks you get your final headcount.\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399410602,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}}],"Id":"79405","Title":"Need To Vent!","LastPostDate":1438089392},"Pages":{"TotalItems":15,"TotalPages":2,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":10,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":10},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
